  "rollback_evidence": "1.0.12 G145 (J31-J33), measured on vJunos-switch 26.2R1.7 (d-vjunos, GNS3 lab on PC-Radek KVM, task-evidence/g145/probe1-3) with the safeguard of the Junos interface profile: an empty 'commit confirmed 10 comment \"netops-<id>\"' first, the change committed with 'commit confirmed 10 comment \"netops-change\"', the confirmation 'commit comment \"netops-<id>-ok\"'; an expiry returns the configuration before the change. The key is the address of the remote syslog host as Junos shows it. Lines: 'set system syslog host <ip> any <severity>' (the level of all facilities), 'set system syslog host <ip> <facility> <severity>' (attribute 'severity-<facility>'; a host keeps at least one of 'any' and the facility levels; the level of one facility; the facilities are the completions of 'set system syslog host <ip> ?': authorization, change-log, conflict-log, daemon, dfc, external, firewall, ftp, interactive-commands, kernel, ntp, pfe, security, user; a set replaces the level of the facility, the other facilities of the host stay), 'set system syslog host <ip> port <p>' and 'set system syslog host <ip> facility-override <facility>' (single values: a set replaces the old one, measured), 'delete system syslog host <ip> port|facility-override|<facility>' and 'delete system syslog host <ip>' (removes the host; deleting its last statement removes it as well). The severities and facilities are the completions of the CLI ('?'). A host with other statements (source-address, match, structured-data ...) is refused; the local syslog files are not touched."
